System.Net.NetworkInformation for witos (plan step W4.2, RFC 0015 section 8): the project targets the unix flavor when
the build is for witos, as System.Net.Http and System.Net.Security do (W2.2), and gives it Linux's files: Linux's PAL
asks System.Native for the interfaces (getifaddrs and the interface ioctls, which the libc answers from the network
service's configuration through its netlink route socket), reads /etc/resolv.conf for the DNS servers and the routes
from /proc/net only where that file exists, so NetworkInterface and NetworkChange work, while the statistics, which Linux
reads from /proc/net, are not kept (Compatibility-Differences: Network interfaces). Without it the assembly built for
witos is the platform-neutral one, whose types throw PlatformNotSupportedException.

